}
```

Wheel handler:
```
let acc=0, lock=false;
el.addEventListener('wheel', e=>{
  e.preventDefault();
  if(lock) return;
  acc += e.deltaY;
  if(Math.abs(acc) >= 60){
    go(idx + (acc>0?1:-1));
    acc = 0;
    lock = true;
    setTimeout(()=>lock=false, 700);
  }
}, {passive:false});
```

Hmm 700ms lock plus transition 900ms. Maybe lock 650. Fine.

But trackpad momentum: after lock releases, residual events could trigger again. 700ms should absorb most. Could also reset acc on lock. OK.

Also I want scrolling to feel fluid: transition 800-1000ms. Use 900.

Also the globe.gl default zoom on wheel: globe.gl's OrbitControls has zoom via wheel by default, which would conflict (zoom in/out). I need to disable zoom via wheel so my handler controls it. Set `world.controls().enableZoom = false;`. That prevents zoom. Good. But then user can't zoom; acceptable. Or keep zoom on ctrl+wheel? Keep it simple: disable enableZoom.

Also disable panning? Panning could move the globe off-center; pointOfView recenters anyway. Keep default rotate drag. I'll set enablePan=false maybe. Leave rotate drag enabled.

Also `.controls().autoRotate` default true; I'll keep spin checkbox.

Now the index indicator: add to HUD or panel. Let me add a small line in the panel header or a separate element. I'll add `#counter` in the panel showing "3 / 27". Or in HUD. Let me add under the count in panel: `<div class="nav" id="pNav">3 / 27</div>`.

Also update the hint text: "Scroll to cycle countries (A→Z)".

Let me also make the panel show even before any click; on load maybe select first country? Not necessary. But scrolling shows it.

Let me also handle: when user clicks a country manually, set idx to that country's index if it's in NAV, and select it. Good for consistency.

Let me also make sure `showPanel` handles countries with 0 (clicked non-data country) — it shows "No geolocated tweets". And set selected to it? If clicked country not in NAV, selected set, but idx unchanged. Fine.

Now update template file and regenerate.

Let me rewrite the template with these changes. I'll edit the existing template file.

Changes:
